{"results":[{"url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2019/08/26/trump-nuclear-weapons-hurricane/","final_url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2019/08/26/trump-nuclear-weapons-hurricane/","title":"Trump denies that he suggested nuking hurricanes. But the government once studied the idea. ","description":"In 1945, the mayor of Miami Beach wrote to President Harry S. Truman to suggest that atomic bombs be used to stop hurricanes in their tracks.","language":"en","text":"Democracy Dies in Darkness\n\nBy  Antonia Noori Farzan\n\nIn October 1935, roughly six weeks after a devastating hurricane laid waste to the Florida Keys, a group of frustrated chamber of commerce executives from the storm-battered cities of Miami, Fort Lauderdale and Hollywood, Fla., got together to figure out what could be done about storms that mercilessly pounded the state’s coast every fall, threatening the burgeoning tourist economy.\n\n---","author":"Antonia Noori Farzan","published_date":"2019-08-26T12:42:52.359Z","latency_ms":1063.2223319998957,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}